---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Can the watermark be removed?',
    a: 'Not here, and not by accident: it is printed into the pages when the file saves. But a determined person with a full PDF editor could still lift it off. That is the honest position: the stamp stops a casual reader mistaking the file, not a determined one copying it. If the file itself must stay shut, put a password on it as well, with the protect tool.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the stamp cover photos and charts too?',
    a: 'Yes. It is drawn over the whole page, across text, photos and charts alike, at the strength you picked. At the light setting it sits under your reading; at the strong setting it is the first thing seen.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long can the stamp be?',
    a: 'Up to 40 characters: a word or a short phrase, like DRAFT, CONFIDENTIAL or DO NOT COPY. The stamp is sized to span the page, so a long sentence would be shrunk to nothing; if you need a paragraph on the file, it belongs in the document, not across it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my document go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is read into this page and watermarked in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to watermark a PDF",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the PDF", text: "Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. The page reads its page count before anything runs." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Write the stamp", text: "Type the words (DRAFT, CONFIDENTIAL, or your own, up to 40 characters), and pick the size, the strength, diagonal or straight, and every page or one range." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Watermark the PDF", text: "Press 'Watermark the PDF'. The words are printed into each chosen page and the file is saved with them inside it." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the watermarked PDF", text: "Take the finished file away, and keep your clean original: this page cannot un-stamp a file." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="Watermark a PDF: stamp DRAFT or your own words across the pages, free · Benchzy" description="Stamp a short text across every page of a PDF, or one range: diagonal or straight, at the size and strength you pick, inside your browser. Stated plainly on the page: a label, not a lock.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">PDF tools · pages</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Watermark PDF</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Stamp one short text (DRAFT, CONFIDENTIAL, or your own words) across the pages of a
        PDF, so anyone who opens it knows what it is. The stamp is printed into the pages
        when the file saves, in your browser; the document is never uploaded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="wm-tool">
      <div id="wm-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PDF">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="wm-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <p class="file-loaded hidden" data-loaded-for="wm-file" role="status"></p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">The stamp</h2>
          <label class="block mt-3 text-sm font-bold" for="wm-text">Words to stamp</label>
          <input id="wm-text" type="text" value="DRAFT" maxlength="40" class="mt-1 w-full border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2" autocomplete="off" />
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">Size</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-size" value="small" />
              <span>Small (about a third of the page across)</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-size" value="medium" checked />
              <span>Medium (over half the page across)</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-size" value="large" />
              <span>Large (most of the page across)</span>
            </label>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">Strength and slant</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-opacity" value="0.15" />
              <span>Light: you read through it</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-opacity" value="0.3" checked />
              <span>Medium: plainly there</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-opacity" value="0.5" />
              <span>Strong: the first thing seen</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-layout" value="diagonal" checked />
              <span>Diagonal, corner to corner</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-layout" value="straight" />
              <span>Straight, across the middle</span>
            </label>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">Which pages</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-scope" value="all" checked />
              <span>Every page</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="wm-scope" value="range" />
              <span>One page range</span>
            </label>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-6 flex-wrap">
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="wm-from">From page</label>
              <input id="wm-from" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="wm-to">To page</label>
              <input id="wm-to" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="wm-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="action-note">
            Read this before you run: the stamp becomes part of the pages, like ink soaked
            into the paper. Keep your clean original; this page cannot un-stamp a file.
          </p>
          <button id="wm-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Watermark the PDF</button>
          <p id="wm-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PDF to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="wm-result" class="receipt hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="wm-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="wm-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="wm-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the watermarked PDF</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For a draft going out for comments, a quote that is not final, or a pack that must not be mistaken for the signed version." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick the PDF' }, { n: '02', t: 'Write the stamp' }, { n: '03', t: 'Watermark and download' }]} />

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The page writes your words onto every page you chose, at the size and strength you
          picked, and saves the file with the words inside it. The download is how we
          protect your privacy: the program that does this job is part of this page, loaded
          from this site, and your file is read into the page and never uploaded. From then
          on the stamp prints and copies with the file, like ink soaked into the paper.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          A watermark is a label, not a lock. It is printed into the page content, which
          means a determined person with a full PDF editor could still lift it off; it
          stops a casual reader mistaking the file, not a determined one copying it. If
          the file itself must stay shut, put a password on it as well, with the
          <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/protect-pdf/">protect tool</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A password-protected PDF cannot be opened by this tool. Take its password off first with the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/unlock-pdf/">unlock tool</a>, then bring the file back.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/watermark-pdf.js';
  </script>
</Base>
